  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "hls_transform_unit",
    "file": "ffmpeg/libavcodec/hevcdec.c",
    "description": "Out-of-bounds read occurs when indexing PPS chroma QP offset tables with an unchecked bitstream-derived index. In hls_transform_unit(), cu_chroma_qp_offset_idx from ff_hevc_cu_chroma_qp_offset_idx(s) is used directly to access s->ps.pps->cb_qp_offset_list[] / cr_qp_offset_list[] at line ~1050, but those arrays have fixed size 5. The PoV drives cu_chroma_qp_offset_idx to 5, causing index 5 OOB (UBSan). Root cause is missing bounds validation/clamping against the table size (and/or configured list length).",
    "conditions": "HEVC bitstream must reach transform parsing with cu_chroma_qp_offset_enabled_flag set, chroma residual path active (cbf_chroma true), not transquant bypass, and chroma QP offset not yet coded, then signal cu_chroma_qp_offset_flag=1 and encode cu_chroma_qp_offset_idx >= 5. Data flow: fuzzer packet -> hevc_decode_frame -> decode_nal_unit(s) -> hls_slice_data -> hls_decode_entry -> hls_coding_quadtree/coding_unit -> hls_transform_tree -> hls_transform_unit, where unchecked cu_chroma_qp_offset_idx indexes the 5-element PPS offset arrays."
  },
